{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381296-spirit-courts-of-the-caul","id":1381296,"title":"Spirit Courts of the Caul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-14T05:48:01-07:00","id":1381296,"title":"Spirit Courts of the Caul","content":"I'm contemplating getting my players to the Caul for their next story, but can't see anything about the spirit courts and/or politics of the area in the Lunar preview.<br /> <br /> I was going for the to be some detail to shelter a god that the Circle have kicked out of their home island for being too bad (kidnapping and killing villages doesn't go down well, even if there are Reasons), so I'm gearing up for a revenge plot.<br /> <br /> One thing that I'm considering is the god petitioning the spirits at the Caul to take the Circle down a poet or two. What do I people think that the Courts at the Caul would look like, and do they support this sort of plot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T17:01:34-07:00","id":1381472,"title":"","content":"Depends which side. I'd imagine that predominantly the Spirit Courts of Caul are aligned with the Silver Pact, outside those based on Faxai. What's the Circle, DBs or Lunars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:26:07-07:00","id":1381690,"title":"","content":"The Circle are Solars, but I was hoping to drag them into the politics of the West as a whole, or at last on a whistlestop tour of a few locations for various reasons. Where they are in the West (close to Lathe) puts them close to where I imagine DB shipping lanes to the Caul would be.<br /> <br /> It's also possible that I don't need to involve the Caul at all, if there are other Spirit Courts I could rope in. But the Caul seems like too good a setting to pass up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T11:25:49-07:00","id":1381712,"title":"","content":"Ah its Solars. Yeah you can work with that.<br /> <br /> Many of the Gods resent the coming of the Lawgivers, since it marks the end of their tyrannies but any case heres some ideas for Caul in particular.<br /> <br /> Since its inception Caul has been very important to only two Exalt types, Lunars and DBs. Even with the conflicts in the present era, I can see any other Exalt activity on the island being looked on as meddling outsiders.the Gods are accustomed to the ways of the Dragons and Moon. Any Solar presence on the island can very much have both sides threatening to come down on them if they believe they are their to take what is theres. Which is an assumption this renegade god could put in in minds of the Spirit Courts, which could filter down to their allies. The Lunars and Dragon-Blooded. This especially becomes pressing if as you said, you intend to have the Circle more involved with the politics of the West. People don't like outsiders, especially for an island which once disappeared from time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:28:29-07:00","id":1381735,"title":"","content":"Not saying you should adhere to this, but if you\u2019re wondering why it isn\u2019t covered in canon, the Realm clarifies that the Caul didn\u2019t come back with gods anymore than it did people, and the Silver Pact has been hostile to anyone assigned there by the Celestial Bureaucracy, seeing them as potential Sid spies. The Caul-born religion focuses on the Caul itself as a living divine entity instead.<br /> <br /> If adding gods to the Caul, I\u2019d play up that they\u2019re eclectic refugees, like terrestrial gods whose original territories got eaten by the Wyld, who have gone out of their way to portray themselves as rogue from Heaven for the comfort of the Lunars who might expel them otherwise. Some minor moon-related deity could serve as go between for the Court and the Pact, since they\u2019ll listen to them out of respect for Luna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T16:15:57-07:00","id":1382263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381296-spirit-courts-of-the-caul?p=1381712#post1381712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many of the Gods resent the coming of the Lawgivers, since it marks the end of their tyrannies...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that depends on the Lawgivers. In my seafaring game, both of the Solar PCs made the Ocean Court <i>stronger</i> in the interest of getting their assistance against the Realm. They built temples, led worship services, and killed a Dragon-Blooded who was using summoned demons to kill local God-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T03:27:46-07:00","id":1382306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381296-spirit-courts-of-the-caul?p=1381712#post1381712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since its inception Caul has been very important to only two Exalt types, Lunars and DBs. Even with the conflicts in the present era, I can see any other Exalt activity on the island being looked on as meddling outsiders.the Gods are accustomed to the ways of the Dragons and Moon. Any Solar presence on the island can very much have both sides threatening to come down on them if they believe they are their to take what is theirs. Which is an assumption this renegade god could put in in minds of the Spirit Courts, which could filter down to their allies. The Lunars and Dragon-Blooded. This especially becomes pressing if as you said, you intend to have the Circle more involved with the politics of the West. People don't like outsiders, especially for an island which once disappeared from time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1381296-spirit-courts-of-the-caul?p=1381735#post1381735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If adding gods to the Caul, I\u2019d play up that they\u2019re eclectic refugees, like terrestrial gods whose original territories got eaten by the Wyld, who have gone out of their way to portray themselves as rogue from Heaven for the comfort of the Lunars who might expel them otherwise. Some minor moon-related deity could serve as go between for the Court and the Pact, since they\u2019ll listen to them out of respect for Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are really neat ideas. A god who had been pushed out of their original purview would also find more support among those who are already refugees, and the presence of Outcaste Dragon-blooded looking to prove themselves could also be something that the god is using as a recruitment tool. Which, if it fails, could then lead the god to turn to the Exigence...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}